IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nl-pit`
IMPORT `nl-pit-notice`

-- Newfoundland and Labrador Income Tax Act, 2000 -- the individual taxpayer's questions, for the 2025 and 2026 taxation
-- years. Every question calls the rules in nl-pit.l4 and nl-pit-notice.l4; nothing is restated. Plain inputs, one per fact
-- the person can state. Federal amounts (taxable income, net income, the CPP and EI base, adjusted income) come from the
-- person's federal return; see the federal Income Tax Act encoding in subjects/ca/income-tax-act/.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Must I pay Newfoundland and Labrador income tax`

@export Must I pay Newfoundland and Labrador income tax for the year under s 6(1) of the Income Tax Act, 2000?
GIVEN `I was resident in Newfoundland and Labrador on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Newfoundland and Labrador on the last day of the taxation year (31 December)
      `I earned income in Newfoundland and Labrador in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while not resident there on 31 December, you had income earned in the year in Newfoundland and Labrador (for example employment there)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay Newfoundland and Labrador income tax` IF
    `the individual must pay income tax under the Act` `I was resident in Newfoundland and Labrador on 31 December` `I earned income in Newfoundland and Labrador in the year`

§ `How much tax do I pay`

@export How much Newfoundland and Labrador tax is charged on my taxable income under s 7 of the Income Tax Act, 2000, before any credit?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation (calendar) year: 2025 or 2026
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year in Canadian dollars, as on your federal return (line 26000)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is the tax on my taxable income` MEANS
    IF `the taxation year is encoded` `the taxation year`
    THEN `answered` (`to the cent` (`the s 7 tax on` `my taxable income` `with thresholds` (`the thresholds for the year` `the taxation year`)))
    ELSE `not covered` `only the 2025 and 2026 taxation years are encoded`

@export How much are my Newfoundland and Labrador personal, age, pension, CPP and EI credits under ss 9 and 17 of the Income Tax Act, 2000?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation (calendar) year: 2025 or 2026
      `what I claim under s 9(1)` IS A `s 9(1) claim` @desc Paragraph (a) if you are married or in a common-law partnership and support your spouse or partner; paragraph (b) if you are single (or separated and unsupported) and keep a home in which you support a related dependant; otherwise paragraph (c)
      `my spouse's or dependant's net income` IS A NUMBER @desc The net income for the year of the spouse, partner or dependant you claim for, in Canadian dollars; 0 if you claim under paragraph (c)
      `the spouse or dependant income threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed income threshold for the year in the s 9(1)(a) and (b) formula (printed in the Act as $606), as shown on the provincial tax form NL428 for the year
      `I am 65 or over by 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reach age 65 before the end of the taxation year
      `my net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for the year in Canadian dollars, as on your federal return (line 23600)
      `the age amount income threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed income threshold for the year in the s 9(2) formula (printed in the Act as $33,226), as shown on form NL428 for the year
      `my pension income amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The eligible pension income you count for the federal pension income amount (federal s 118(3)), in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my CPP contributions and EI premiums for the credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the employee CPP contributions and EI premiums that count for the federal s 118.7 credit, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What are my personal credits` MEANS
    IF `the taxation year is encoded` `the taxation year`
    THEN `answered` (`to the cent` `the total`)
    ELSE `not covered` `only the 2025 and 2026 taxation years are encoded`
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `the credit amounts for the year` `the taxation year`
        `s 9(1)` MEANS `the s 9(1) amount` `what I claim under s 9(1)` amounts `the spouse or dependant income threshold` `my spouse's or dependant's net income`
        `s 9(2)` MEANS `the s 9(2) amount` `I am 65 or over by 31 December` (amounts's `age amount`) `the age amount income threshold` `my net income`
        `s 9(3)` MEANS `the s 9(3) amount` `my pension income amount`
        `the total` MEANS (`the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`s 9(1)` PLUS `s 9(2)` PLUS `s 9(3)`)) PLUS (`the s 17 credit` `my CPP contributions and EI premiums for the credit`)

@export How much Newfoundland and Labrador income tax do I pay after the tax on taxable income, my personal credits and the low income reduction?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation (calendar) year: 2025 or 2026
      `I was resident in Newfoundland and Labrador on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Newfoundland and Labrador on 31 December of the year
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year in Canadian dollars, as on your federal return (line 26000)
      `my personal credits` IS A NUMBER @desc Your provincial personal, age, pension, CPP and EI credits, in dollars (see the credits question)
      `my family's adjusted income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income plus that of your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, if any, in Canadian dollars
      `I have a spouse or claim an eligible dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at the end of the year you had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, or you claim the eligible dependant amount under s 9(1)(b)
      `low income reduction amount A` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount A prescribed by regulation for the year under s 21.1(2.1)(a) ($974 for 2024 under NLR 60/24), from form NL428 for the year
      `low income reduction amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount B prescribed by regulation for the year under s 21.1(2.1)(b) ($544 for 2024), from form NL428 for the year
      `low income reduction single threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed s 21.1(2)(b) income threshold for the year (printed in the Act as $18,547)
      `low income reduction family threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed s 21.1(2)(c) income threshold for the year (printed in the Act as $31,362)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Newfoundland and Labrador income tax do I pay` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the taxation year is encoded` `the taxation year`)
    THEN `not covered` `only the 2025 and 2026 taxation years are encoded`
    ELSE IF NOT (`I was resident in Newfoundland and Labrador on 31 December`)
         THEN `not covered` `only an individual resident in the province on the last day of the taxation year is encoded`
         ELSE LET `after credits` MEANS `the tax after the personal credits` (`the s 7 tax on` `my taxable income` `with thresholds` (`the thresholds for the year` `the taxation year`)) `my personal credits`
                  `reduction` MEANS `the s 21.1 reduction` TRUE `I have a spouse or claim an eligible dependant` `my family's adjusted income` `low income reduction amount A` `low income reduction amount B` `low income reduction single threshold` `low income reduction family threshold`
              IN  `answered` (`to the cent` (`the tax after the low income reduction` `after credits` `reduction`))

@export How much is my Newfoundland and Labrador low income reduction under s 21.1 of the Income Tax Act, 2000?
GIVEN `my family's adjusted income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income plus that of your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, if any, in Canadian dollars
      `I have a spouse or claim an eligible dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at the end of the year you had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, or you claim the eligible dependant amount under s 9(1)(b)
      `low income reduction amount A` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount A prescribed for the year under s 21.1(2.1)(a) ($974 for 2024 under NLR 60/24)
      `low income reduction amount B` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount B prescribed for the year under s 21.1(2.1)(b) ($544 for 2024 under NLR 60/24)
      `low income reduction single threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed s 21.1(2)(b) income threshold for the year (printed in the Act as $18,547)
      `low income reduction family threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed s 21.1(2)(c) income threshold for the year (printed in the Act as $31,362)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my low income reduction` MEANS
    `to the cent` (`the s 21.1 reduction` TRUE `I have a spouse or claim an eligible dependant` `my family's adjusted income` `low income reduction amount A` `low income reduction amount B` `low income reduction single threshold` `low income reduction family threshold`)

§ `What is paid back to me -- the income supplement and seniors' benefit`

@export How much Newfoundland and Labrador income supplement and seniors' benefit do I get for a taxation year, in total, under s 34 and NLR 32/16?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation year whose return the benefit is based on: 2025 or 2026 (paid in July and October of the next year and January and April of the year after)
      `my family's adjusted income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income plus that of your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, if any, for the taxation year, in Canadian dollars
      `I have a cohabiting spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner (your qualified relation)
      `my qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualified dependants (children under 19 living with you, as for the GST/HST credit) you have
      `I can claim the disability tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for the federal disability tax credit (s 118.3(1))
      `my spouse can claim the disability tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cohabiting spouse or partner is eligible for the federal disability tax credit
      `I am 64 or over in the taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are 64 years of age or over at any time in the taxation year
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much income supplement and seniors' benefit do I get in the year` MEANS
    IF `the taxation year is encoded` `the taxation year`
    THEN `answered` (`to the cent` (`supplement` PLUS `disability` PLUS `seniors`))
    ELSE `not covered` `only the 2025 and 2026 taxation years are encoded`
    WHERE
        `supplement` MEANS `the income supplement` `my family's adjusted income` `I have a cohabiting spouse or partner` `my qualified dependants`
        `disability` MEANS `the disability amount` `my family's adjusted income` `I can claim the disability tax credit` `my spouse can claim the disability tax credit`
        `seniors` MEANS `the seniors' benefit` `my family's adjusted income` `I am 64 or over in the taxation year`

@export How much of my yearly Newfoundland and Labrador income supplement and seniors' benefit is paid in each of the four specified months (s 34(3))?
GIVEN `my yearly total` IS A NUMBER @desc Your yearly total of the income supplement and seniors' benefit (see the previous question), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is paid each quarter` MEANS `each specified month's amount` `my yearly total`

@export Is my whole year's Newfoundland and Labrador income supplement paid in one amount, in the first specified month, because each quarterly payment would be under $10 (s 34(10), (11))?
GIVEN `my yearly total` IS A NUMBER @desc Your yearly total of the income supplement and seniors' benefit, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it paid in one amount` IF `paid in one amount in the first specified month` `my yearly total`

§ `Telling the Canada Revenue Agency about a change`

-- Arises only when the person's family situation changes while receiving the supplement.

@export Must I tell the Minister of National Revenue (the Canada Revenue Agency) about this change under s 34(8) of the Income Tax Act, 2000?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `s 34(8) event` @desc What changed: you stopped being an eligible individual; someone became or stopped being your cohabiting spouse or partner; a child stopped being your qualified dependant other than by turning 19; or a child turned 19
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the CRA about the change` IF `the event must be notified` `what happened`

@export By what date must I tell the Minister of National Revenue about the change under s 34(8)?
GIVEN `the date of the change` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the change happened
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I tell the CRA` MEANS `the last day of the month following` `the date of the change`
